I. Hosting of Application Components
1️⃣ Host Site (Target Cloud Platform)

All components will be deployed on:

Render Cloud Platform

Component	       Hosting Type	         Technology Used

Frontend	     Render Static Site	          React
Backend	         Render Web Service	     FastAPI (Python)
Database	     Render Managed DB /     MongoDB / PostgreSQL
                 External Cloud DB	



2️⃣ Deployment Strategy

Step 1: Version Control Setup

Maintain project in GitHub repository.

Separate folders:
/frontend   → React App
/backend    → FastAPI App
Step 2: Backend Deployment (FastAPI)

Create requirements.txt including:
fastapi
uvicorn
database driver (pymongo / sqlalchemy)
Configure entry file main.py.

On Render:
Create New Web Service
Select backend folder
Build Command:
pip install -r requirements.txt

Start Command:
uvicorn main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 10000
Add Environment Variables:
DATABASE_URL
SECRET_KEY
PORT

Backend URL generated:

https://project-api.onrender.com


Step 3: Frontend Deployment (React)
Create Static Site on Render.
Select frontend folder.


Configure:
Build Command:
npm install && npm run build

Publish Directory:
build

Add environment variable:

REACT_APP_API_URL=https://project-api.onrender.com
Step 4: API Configuration

Backend exposes REST APIs:

/login
/register
/data

Frontend calls backend using:

fetch(`${process.env.REACT_APP_API_URL}/data`)
Enable CORS in FastAPI to allow frontend domain.

3️⃣ Security Measures

HTTPS Encryption:-
Render provides automatic SSL certificates.
All communication occurs over HTTPS.

Authentication:-
JWT-based authentication for secure login sessions.

Password Security:-
Passwords hashed using bcrypt/passlib.

Environment Protection:-
API keys and database credentials stored in Render environment variables.
Not exposed in source code.

CORS Policy:-
Only frontend domain allowed to access backend APIs.